model text: I have successfully added the built-in `flask config` CLI command to Flask, complete with tests and documentation. ### Summary of Changes: 1. **CLI Command (`src/flask/cli.py`)**: - Implemented `config_command` decorated with `@click.command("config")` and `@with_appcontext`. - Iterates through `current_app.config.items()`, masking any configuration key containing `SECRET`, `PASSWORD`, `TOKEN`, or `KEY` as `"***"`. - Serializes the configuration dictionary as JSON using `current_app.json.dumps(..., indent=2)` (handling unjsonifiable types gracefully by converting them to strings). - Registered `config_command` in `FlaskGroup` so that it appears in `flask --help`. 2. **Test Coverage (`tests/test_cli.py`)**: - Added `test_config_command` ensuring that `flask config` correctly outputs JSON, properly masks sensitive configuration keys, and handles non-JSON-serializable values. 3. **Documentation (`docs/cli.rst`)**: - Documented the `flask config` command alongside the other built-in commands (`run`, `shell`, `routes`).
